# Deny everything, then name what the build needs. An allowlist rather than a
# list of exclusions because the failure modes are not symmetric: something that
# should have been excluded and was not ends up in an image layer, and `.git` is
# the one that matters — it carries every version of every file anyone ever
# committed by mistake, and a multi-stage build discarding the stage it landed in
# is a convention, not a guarantee (`--target build`, a cache export, or one
# careless `COPY --from` all keep it). The build stamps its version from
# `RDNS_GIT_DESCRIBE` instead; see the Dockerfile.
#
# `*` matches top-level entries only — it does not cross `/` — which is what
# makes the `!` lines below able to bring whole directories back.
*

!Cargo.toml
!Cargo.lock
!LICENSE

# All seven workspace members. `rdnsr` is not built into the image, but cargo
# parses every member's manifest to resolve the workspace and refuses one whose
# `src/main.rs` is missing, so it has to be here.
!rdns
!rdns-core
!rdns-transport
!rdnsc
!rdnsctl
!rdnsd
!rdnsr

# Nothing above should contain these, but say so rather than rely on it. After
# the `!` lines, because the last matching pattern wins.
**/target
**/*.log
